<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================

  Wires the RULED fauna roster for the Pyrelands into RM_Pyrelands'
  wildAnimals, replacing the deliberate core-only vanilla placeholder that
  src/RimMandrake/Pyrelands/Defs/BiomeDefs/Pyrelands.xml ships (Hare, Rat,
  Gazelle, Ostrich, Emu, Dromedary, Muffalo, Iguana, Elephant, Rhinoceros,
  Cougar, Fox_Fennec, Warg — kept there so the Pyrelands mod is self-contained
  and works with nothing else loaded). The wiring lives HERE, in UtinniPatches,
  never in the Pyrelands mod itself — that mod must stay standalone.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: every defName and every commonality number below is
  copied verbatim from design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/
  the_pyrelands.json's "fauna" array (authored 2026-09-09, owner-ruled sitting
  entries through 2026-09-10 — the GR_ correction pass, the
  PYRELANDS_FIRE_WEB_COMMISSION_1 igniter builds, and the round-2 move-mapping
  import of Dalgo) — NOT re-derived or rescaled here. That JSON
  is the actual ruling; this file only wires it into the def the game reads.
  The 14-animal sum is 4.91 (RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-20 against the weights actually
  written below) — not the placeholder's ~5.8, a deliberate consequence of using
  the owner's real per-species numbers rather than matching the placeholder's
  total. (This comment previously said 4.21, stale from before Dalgo's round-2
  import and the PYRELANDS_DONOR_PORT_4 rename pass; nothing below changed.)

  ⚠️ The JSON records the owner's RULINGS, and several of its rows still name the
  donor defName that carried the ruled creature at the time he ruled. Every one
  of those has since been re-authored as our own def at the SAME commonality; the
  operations below are the current mapping and are the authority on WHICH def is
  cast. The weights are still the JSON's, unchanged.

  🔴 2026-09-14 (BOOMALOPE_CUT_EVERYWHERE_1): vanilla Boomalope, originally
  wired here 2026-09-13 under the 2026-09-09 KEEP-reskinned card, is cut —
  owner ruling "Absolutely no boomalopes," reversing that card. Removed from
  the unconditional block and the roster below; counts corrected to 14/4.21.

  🔴 2026-09-16 (FLAMEFANG_SNAKE_REBIRTH_1): the venom-ambusher is the flamefang
  — owner sheet note, verbatim: "rename this to Flamefang and make it venomous,"
  which postdates and supersedes BOOMSNAKE_CUT_CONFLICT_1 (2026-09-14, which had
  un-wired the creature after finding no ruling had ever restored it
  post-BOOM_FAMILY_CUT_1). It is a distinct venom-ambush niche, not the
  fire-follower niche — that is the sytheclaw's, per the 2026-09-14 recast.

  🔴 2026-09-19 (PYRELANDS_DONOR_PORT_4): every creature this file casts is now
  one of OUR defs. The four that still rode a donor defName — GR_Boomsnake,
  AA_Razorjack, AA_Barbslinger, AA_FireWasp — were re-authored as RUT_Flamefang,
  RUT_Sytheclaw, RUT_Barbslinger and RUT_FireWasp in
  Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml, carrying their own labels
  and descriptions, so the two identity patches (FlamefangIdentity.xml,
  RazorjackIdentity_Sytheclaw.xml), the venom-rewiring patch (FlamefangVenom.xml)
  and the four ArtOverride mods are all deleted — git is the provenance. The
  Cherry Picker ThingDef cut on GR_Boomsnake is now irrelevant rather than
  reversed: nothing casts that def any more.

  🔑 STRUCTURE: one PatchOperationConditional-guarded PatchOperationReplace
  swaps the WHOLE node for the two commissioned igniters (both always
  loaded — this mod's own defs). Two more PatchOperationConditional blocks then
  splice the rest in via PatchOperationAdd on the now-existing node,
  shorthand-dictionary form throughout — the whole biome's own wildAnimals list
  already uses that form (`<Hare>1.2</Hare>` etc.), and it is the ONLY form
  BiomeAnimalRecord.LoadDataFromXmlCustom reads (same mechanism as
  WeatherCommonalityRecord — see this mod's AshStorms_Pyrelands.xml for the
  measured citation). There is no PatchOperationFindMod left in this file: every
  def cast here is ours, so the only gate that makes sense is the one on the
  BIOME's own mod.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional returns
  true on no match) — validated with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def dump
  and the full active mod set; see the file-level record for the verdict.

  ============================================================================
  ROSTER AND VERIFICATION
  ============================================================================

  UNCONDITIONAL (this mod's own defs — always loaded):
    RUT_FireHawk       0.15  igniter-flier      — RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml (this mod)
    RUT_FurnaceBeast   0.08  igniter-megafauna  — RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml (this mod)

  OURS, re-authored off a donor defName (PYRELANDS_DONOR_PORT_4, 2026-09-19 —
  Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml, always loaded with this mod):
    RUT_Sytheclaw      0.20  fire-follower      — was AA_Razorjack   (Alpha Animals)
    RUT_Barbslinger    0.15  ash-grazer         — was AA_Barbslinger (Alpha Animals)
    RUT_FireWasp       0.40  small-predator     — was AA_FireWasp    (Alpha Animals)
    RUT_Flamefang      0.50  venom-ambush       — was GR_Boomsnake   (Vanilla Genetics Expanded)

  OURS, re-authored off a dead donor defName (EMBERSCYTHE_MANTIS_REAUTHOR_1,
  rehomed into this mod by EMBERSCYTHE_PYRELANDS_REHOME_1 2026-09-19 —
  src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_Emberscythe.xml):
    RUT_Emberscythe    0.05  large-predator     — was GR_Mantistanis (Vanilla Genetics Expanded)

  Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued) (mod name string "Star Wars Animal
  Collection (Continued)", packageId mlie.starwarsanimalcollection — confirmed
  active in ModsConfig.xml). This mod's own workshop download was not present
  in the local Steam Workshop cache to cite a raw XML line directly (only a
  dependent mod, "Star Wars : The Force Standalone", id 3557220601, was found,
  and it does not itself declare these races). Verified instead via TWO
  independent lines of evidence that both require these exact defNames to be
  real, loaded PawnKindDefs sourced from this mod:
    (a) design/Jawa/fauna/animal_census.csv:487,493,515,549,583,585,637 —
        Gizka/Anooba/Dalgo/Iriaz/Nuna/Orray/Zeer, each row's `mod`/`packageId`
        columns naming this exact mod, built from a live per-mod XML scan.
    (b) src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml —
        this repo's OWN live fix, confirmed firing against a real capture, for
        `/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/wildAnimals/Iriaz[2]`
        (that file's op #40) and (per that file's header) prior removals for
        Gizka/Nuna/Orray/Zeer duplicate records against the same biome — a
        PatchOperationConditional that fires proves the exact node existed in
        the loaded def set, not merely in this mod's own claim.
    Anooba is the bare "Anooba" defName from Star Wars Animal Collection
    (Continued), NOT this repo's own RSW_Anooba port
    (src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_Anooba.xml) — that
    port is a distinct def created only to resolve a ZBiome_Grasslands/
    Ashkarr duplicate-record collision and is not wired to any other biome by
    that change.
    Anooba              0.35  medium-predator
    Iriaz               0.50  small-herd
    Nuna                0.50  small
    Orray               0.25  medium (burrower + predator double role)
    Zeer                0.60  large-herd
    Dalgo               0.18  brake (round-2 import)
    Gizka               1.00  grain (ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1: the most-seen animal)

  ============================================================================
  LEFT OUT: vanilla Boomalope only (BOOMALOPE_CUT_EVERYWHERE_1, 2026-09-14).
  Every other name in the item's checklist and in the_pyrelands.json's ruled
  "fauna" array is cast above, as one of our own defs. Gizka is wired although
  it is not in the item's own checklist, because the item's brief was to wire
  "the ruled fauna roster" and the JSON is that roster; leaving it out would
  silently under-wire a roster the owner already ruled complete.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Always: replace the vanilla core-only placeholder with the two
       commissioned igniters (vanilla Boomalope was cut, BOOMALOPE_CUT_EVERYWHERE_1,
       2026-09-14 — not in the value below). Unconditional on any DONOR mod — both
       defNames are this mod's own, always loaded whenever UtinniPatches is — but
       still PatchOperationConditional-guarded on the target node itself, so this
       becomes a silent no-op rather than a red launch error in the (currently
       impossible, but not worth risking) case that the Pyrelands mod is ever
       removed while UtinniPatches stays in. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildAnimals>
          <RUT_FireHawk>0.15</RUT_FireHawk>
          <RUT_FurnaceBeast>0.08</RUT_FurnaceBeast>
        </wildAnimals>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- The SW-canon herd, Anooba as a second flame-edge hunter, and Gizka as the
       quick grain-forager — all SEVEN as OUR OWN defs.
       Owner's ruling 2026-09-19, verbatim: "They should be using OUR creatures, not
       the donor references. The donor references, if any, should never be used
       again." This block previously cast the donor's bare <Anooba>/<Iriaz>/<Nuna>/
       <Orray>/<Zeer>/<Dalgo>/<Gizka> behind a FindMod on the donor mod. All seven
       exist as RSW_ ports in SWBestiary (MEASURED 2026-09-19), so the donor keys are
       gone and the gate moved with them: a FindMod on the DONOR would have dropped
       OUR creatures out of the Pyrelands if that mod were ever removed.
       Weights are the ones authored for this biome and are unchanged. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Anooba>0.35</RSW_Anooba>
        <RSW_Iriaz>0.5</RSW_Iriaz>
        <RSW_Nuna>0.5</RSW_Nuna>
        <RSW_Orray>0.25</RSW_Orray>
        <RSW_Zeer>0.6</RSW_Zeer>
        <RSW_Dalgo>0.18</RSW_Dalgo>
        <RSW_Gizka>1.0</RSW_Gizka>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- OUR OWN Pyrelands fauna, each at the exact weight the donor it replaced held.
       RUT_Emberscythe re-authors GR_Mantistanis (0.05) — EMBERSCYTHE_MANTIS_REAUTHOR_1;
       owner 2026-09-19: "YES for Pyrelands and no elsewhere." The other four are
       PYRELANDS_DONOR_PORT_4, owner 2026-09-19, verbatim: "The flamefang should be
       added to the biome and any donors cut, period. Let's be done with these
       lingering traces," then "port all four":
         RUT_Sytheclaw   0.2   was AA_Razorjack   (Alpha Animals)
         RUT_Barbslinger 0.15  was AA_Barbslinger (Alpha Animals)
         RUT_FireWasp    0.4   was AA_FireWasp    (Alpha Animals)
         RUT_Flamefang   0.5   was GR_Boomsnake   (Vanilla Genetics Expanded)
       All five are UtinniPatches' own defs (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml,
       RUT_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml, RUT_Emberscythe.xml — the last rehomed off
       RotSporeKit by EMBERSCYTHE_PYRELANDS_REHOME_1, 2026-09-19), so the gate is
       the BIOME's mod and nothing else — the two donor FindMod blocks that used to sit
       here are gone, and with them the last reason this file could lose a creature to a
       donor mod being unsubscribed. Casting HERE, with the rest of the Pyrelands cast,
       rather than in BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml — one biome, one file. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.pyrelands">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Pyrelands"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RUT_Emberscythe>0.05</RUT_Emberscythe>
        <RUT_Sytheclaw>0.2</RUT_Sytheclaw>
        <RUT_Barbslinger>0.15</RUT_Barbslinger>
        <RUT_FireWasp>0.4</RUT_FireWasp>
        <RUT_Flamefang>0.5</RUT_Flamefang>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
